        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): verify completion delivery target",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nThis PR tightens ACP/subagent completion announcement delivery accounting so a completion is only counted as visibly delivered when the delivery evidence matches the requester route.\n\nIt:\n- propagates outbound payload target metadata into delivery status\n- validates automatic completion delivery against provider/account/channel/thread targets\n- requires exact account/thread evidence for threaded origins\n- preserves target metadata on failed payload outcomes for diagnostics\n- keeps the current-chat generated-media compatibility path while avoiding explicit wrong-target matches\n\n## Behavior addressed\n\nCompletion announcements can be injected through an internal/inter-session path while the original requester is a channel/thread. Broad checks such as “visible payload exists” or “message tool sent something” can count delivery as successful even when the visible delivery evidence belongs to another route.\n\nThis change makes completion delivery proof target-aware: wrong thread, missing thread, missing account, and provider mismatches no longer satisfy delivery for a concrete requester route.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior addressed**: Completion delivery is only counted as visibly delivered when runtime delivery evidence matches the requester route, including concrete account/thread target. Wrong-thread message-tool evidence must be rejected; exact-thread evidence must be accepted.\n- **Real setup tested**: Disposable checkout of PR branch `anyech/openclaw:fix/acp-completion-thread-delivery` under `tmp/github-open-work/real-proof-20260603T073207Z/pr-89287`. A one-off non-production runtime harness (`proof-89287.ts`, saved in the review artifact directory and disposable checkout) imported the real `src/agents/subagent-announce-delivery.ts` module and called `deliverSubagentAnnouncement` through the real announce dispatch/direct-delivery path. Synthetic session store/config/origin data used a fake Discord group/thread route; only the boundary gateway/transport deps were substituted to record and return delivery envelopes. No production Gateway/config/runtime/state or private deployment proof was used.\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch**: Terminal commands run in the disposable checkout were `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts` and `node --import tsx proof-89287.ts`; full command transcript is in `review/real-proof-build-20260603T073207Z/messaging/exact-commands-used.txt`.\n- **Evidence after fix**: Terminal output / runtime log excerpt from `review/real-proof-build-20260603T073207Z/messaging/evidence/proof-89287.log`:\n\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"agentParams\": {\"deliver\":false,\"channel\":\"discord\",\"to\":\"channel:proof-parent\",\"threadId\":\"thread-proof-expected\",\"sourceReplyDeliveryMode\":\"message_tool_only\"},\n    \"wrong\": {\"delivered\":false,\"path\":\"direct\",\"reason\":\"message_tool_delivery_missing\",\"error\":\"completion agent did not use the message tool for message-tool-only delivery\"},\n    \"correct\": {\"delivered\":true,\"path\":\"direct\",\"phases\":[{\"phase\":\"direct-primary\",\"delivered\":true,\"path\":\"direct\"}]}\n  }\n  ```\n\n- **Observed result after fix**: With the same synthetic requester route, message-tool evidence for `thread-proof-wrong` was rejected/flagged as missing target delivery, while message-tool evidence for `thread-proof-expected` was accepted as direct completion delivery. This exercised the repository runtime announce/direct-delivery implementation, not only an isolated matcher function.\n- **What was not tested**: No live production Gateway, live Discord workspace, real bot token, or private deployment state was used. The outbound provider and gateway agent call were substituted only at the non-production boundary so the proof remains sanitized.\n",
